        "explanation": "Closed geometries naturally support shared branch modes and coherent recirculation."
      },
      {
        "constraint": "requires_nontrivial_topology",
        "weight": 0.7,
        "status": "likely",
        "explanation": "A twisted or nontrivial closed topology is a plausible way to keep theta23 large while preventing theta13 from blowing up."
